  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency drought response through provision of integrated water, sanitation and hygiene promotion (WASH) services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $1.5 million IOM project is to avert further displacement and disease outbreaks by way of providing access to clean drinking water as well as hygiene promotion activities. To that end, IOM will provide water that is safe for consumption through emergency water trucking, construct and rehabilitate critical sanitation infrastructure such as latrines and handwashing stations, provide hygiene kits to 54,000 people and conduct hygiene promotion campaigns, among other life-saving activities. In total, IOM will reach 60,000 people, a majority of which has been displaced, including 12,000 women, 39,000 children and 600 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
